              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BennyMac"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make mine with Hidden valley ranch instead of Mayo, is a friend and family favorite! People always ask why it tastes so good",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-26T19:55:09.387Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GeeQTmom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful Salad! Our family is eating vegetarian (ovo/lacto); so we left out the bacon and subbed in raisins for the texture and extra touch of sweetness. No one missed the bacon and we’re looking forward to leftovers for dinner tonight! Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-22T18:48:42.860Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy Shoge"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I could not stop eating this dish, I loved it so much! This is a great base recipe because you can tailor it to your tastes and it will come out wonderful every time! \n\nI didn't have all the exact ingredients, so I made some substitutions and I also added some ingredients. I made a cole-slaw dressing instead (light mayo, milk, sugar, red wine vinegar); I only had dried, chopped onions and onion powder; the bacon I had was \"maple\" flavored which added a great richness and sweetness to the flavor; I added honey-roasted almond slices and plumped raisins (just soak them in super hot tap water for 3-5 mins); also, I only had the frozen broccoli and cauliflower, so I steamed them first to get them soft, then chilled the whole dish. Lastly, we were curious about how the dish would taste warm so we heated up the last couple bites and it was even better! I'm making it hot next time, I can't wait!",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-20T19:30:21.913Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SnappyToast7722"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for a potluck tomorrow - looking for something on the side in the veggie family. Tastes great and looks great! Some changes I made include: I may have skimped just a tad on the sugar and I used chopped up pecans. Also did 8, not 12 bacon (low sodium) slices. I thought the amount of salad dressing was just right - no changes there.",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-19T18:19:01.651Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cathy D"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is so good and is easy in that it tastes even better if made a day ahead. I used very large heads of cauliflower and broccoli, and substituted craisins for the seeds. Made 50% more of the mayo dressing, so it was nice and creamy, and left everything else the same. Don't leave out the bacon; it makes the salad. I brought it to a party and had two of the 6 women give me their email addresses so they could get the recipe. It was the only dish brought to the gathering that was completely devoured. Highly recommend.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-18T19:01:14.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
